me:concept_Institutional_Reform
    owl:sameAs wd:Q11943714 ;
    skos:scopeNote """Specifically refers to the deconstruction of Taiwan's film censorship system in the 1980s, as well as the structural and legal transformation of the film industry.""" .

me:concept_Urban_Life
    owl:sameAs lcsh:sh85026255 ;
    skos:scopeNote """Refers specifically to the metropolitan lifestyle of Taipei's middle class as portrayed in Edward Yang's films, characterized by a striking contrast between material abundance and spiritual emptiness.""" .

me:concept_alienation
    owl:sameAs lcsh:sh85003542 .

me:concept_humanism
    owl:sameAs wd:Q46158 ;
    schema:isBasedOn me:item_analects ;
    skos:scopeNote """The core philosophical foundation of director Edward Yang's work lies in a profound humanistic concern for individual moral integrity, the dignity of life, and universal humanity, all expressed through a stark and rational audiovisual language.""" .

me:concept_urban_modernity
    owl:sameAs lcsh:sh85026469 ;
    skos:scopeNote """Refers specifically to the rapid urbanization and capitalization process in Taipei City following its economic takeoff at the end of the 20th century.""" .

